1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:07,123
Before anything had a name, there was an ocean of milk, and on it, a serpent with no end.

2
00:00:07,450 --> 00:00:09,916
Ananta: the endless one.

3
00:00:10,250 --> 00:00:17,600
On its coils, Vishnu rests: the preserver, with Lakshmi at his feet, the goddess of good fortune.

4
00:00:17,850 --> 00:00:24,718
His name is often read as the one who pervades everything. The sky and the ocean are his colour.

5
00:00:25,050 --> 00:00:32,246
He holds a conch, a discus, a mace, and a lotus, and he rides on Garuda, king of the birds.

6
00:00:36,050 --> 00:00:42,398
Garuda is the enemy of every serpent, and still he carries the god who sleeps on one.

7
00:00:44,850 --> 00:00:52,072
When the world falls out of balance, Vishnu comes down to set it right. Once, he came as a dwarf.

8
00:00:53,850 --> 00:01:01,584
Vamana asked the great king Bali for a small gift: only as much land as he could cover in three steps.

9
00:01:02,250 --> 00:01:06,530
The king laughed, and agreed. And the dwarf began to grow.

10
00:01:11,850 --> 00:01:14,861
With his first step, he covered the earth.

11
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:18,009
With his second step, the heavens.

12
00:01:19,450 --> 00:01:24,849
There was nowhere left for the third. So Bali bowed, and offered his own head.

13
00:01:29,050 --> 00:01:36,792
In the far south, the city of Thiruvananthapuram takes its name from him: the city of the endless serpent.

14
00:01:36,850 --> 00:01:45,254
In its great temple, Padmanabhaswamy, he lies at rest, so long that he can only be seen through three doors.

15
00:01:47,250 --> 00:01:55,889
In the Bhagavad Gita, as Krishna, he makes a promise: whenever goodness declines, I come again, age after age.

16
00:02:04,250 --> 00:02:12,999
And some say he is closer than that. In a Himalayan river in Nepal, pilgrims gather black stones marked with spirals.

17
00:02:13,450 --> 00:02:23,010
They are ammonites, sea creatures turned to stone some 150 million years ago, honoured as Vishnu himself: the shaligram.

18
00:02:42,850 --> 00:02:49,296
An ocean, a step, a stone. The one who pervades everything, in a line without an end.
